The miner now breaks ties between mempool transactions with equal fee rate (and, under `NextNonceWithHighestFeeRate`, equal nonce rank) by the order in which this node first received them over p2p push, `POST /v2/transactions` or mempool sync, instead of by unspecified database order (admission order or sender address). Of two conflicting transactions (same origin and nonce) at equal fee, the mempool now keeps the earlier-received one, reporting a new `ReplaceByArrival` drop reason to event observers.
